From: Lars Wikman <lars@underjord.io>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: apq8016_sbc: size the SLIMBUS_0_TX backend by the codec TX ports

The SLIMBUS_0_TX backend fixup only set channels->min = 1. The COPP that
q6routing opens for the backend takes params_channels(), which is the
interval's min, so the backend always ran mono however many codec TX
ports were routed into AIF1_CAP. With the two digital mics of a
Fairphone 3 on SLIM TX7 and TX8 the codec sent two SLIMbus channels and
the AFE port was configured for two (q6slim_set_channel_map), but the
COPP was mono and the ADSP copied the first mic into both front-end
channels: a two-channel capture came back with bit-identical channels.

Set the backend channel count to the number of TX ports the codec
reports, the same number the AFE port is configured with, falling back
to mono when the codec has no map.

---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/apq8016_sbc.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/apq8016_sbc.c
@@ -406,8 +406,28 @@
 		channels->min = 1;
 		if (channels->max > 2)
 			channels->max = 2;
-	} else if (cpu_dai->id == SLIMBUS_0_TX ||
-		   cpu_dai->id == TERTIARY_MI2S_TX)
+	} else if (cpu_dai->id == SLIMBUS_0_TX) {
+		/*
+		 * The BE channel count has to be the number of codec TX ports
+		 * routed into the capture DAI ("AIF1_CAP Mixer SLIM TX7" and
+		 * "SLIM TX8" for the two mics): that is how many SLIMbus
+		 * channels the codec sends and how many the AFE port is
+		 * configured with by q6slim_set_channel_map(). The COPP that
+		 * q6routing opens takes params_channels(), which reads the
+		 * interval's min, so only setting min = 1 opened a mono COPP
+		 * for a two-port capture and the ADSP copied the first port
+		 * into every FE channel.
+		 */
+		struct snd_soc_dai *codec_dai = snd_soc_rtd_to_codec(rtd, 0);
+		unsigned int tx_ch[8];
+		unsigned int tx_num = 0;
+
+		if (snd_soc_dai_get_channel_map(codec_dai, &tx_num, tx_ch,
+						NULL, NULL) ||
+		    tx_num < 1 || tx_num > 4)
+			tx_num = 1;
+		channels->min = channels->max = tx_num;
+	} else if (cpu_dai->id == TERTIARY_MI2S_TX)
 		channels->min = 1;
 	else
 		channels->min = channels->max = 2;
